  - question: How much does gutter cleaning cost in Huntsville?
    answer: "<p>Gutter cleaning in Huntsville typically costs $100-200 for most single-story homes and $150-300 for two-story homes, depending on linear footage, roof accessibility, and debris level. Multi-story homes or those with complex rooflines may cost more. We provide exact quotes before starting work.</p>"
  - question: How often should I clean my Huntsville gutters?
    answer: "<p>Most Huntsville homes need cleaning twice yearly — once in late fall after the leaves drop and once in late spring after pollen season and seed pods. Homes surrounded by pine trees may need quarterly cleaning due to year-round needle drop. Homes in newer subdivisions with fewer mature trees may only need annual cleaning.</p>"
  - question: What happens if I don't clean my gutters?
    answer: "<p>Clogged gutters overflow, sending water cascading down your siding and pooling around your foundation. In Huntsville's clay soil, that water doesn't absorb — it sits there, eventually causing foundation cracks, basement flooding, fascia rot, and landscape erosion. In winter, clogged gutters can form ice dams that damage your roof. Foundation repairs cost $10,000-30,000; gutter cleaning costs a fraction of that.</p>"
  - question: Do you repair damage found during cleaning?
