{% set local_problem %}
<p>Huntsville's mature tree coverage is one of the city's best features — and one of the biggest challenges for homeowners. From the historic neighborhoods of Five Points and Twickenham to Monte Sano's wooded lots, Huntsville gutters face constant assault from leaves, pine needles, twigs, and debris.</p>

<p>The numbers tell the story: Huntsville receives 55+ inches of rain annually. When gutters clog, that water doesn't disappear — it overflows, runs down your siding, and pools around your foundation. Huntsville sits on Madison County's notorious red clay soil, which doesn't absorb water. Instead, it directs that water straight toward the path of least resistance — often your basement or crawlspace.</p>

<p>We see it every spring and fall: homeowners dealing with water damage that started with clogged gutters they meant to clean "next weekend." Foundation repairs in Huntsville can cost $10,000-30,000. Basement waterproofing adds thousands more. Regular gutter cleaning costs a tiny fraction of that — and prevents the problem entirely.</p>

<p>For the engineers, scientists, and professionals working at Redstone Arsenal and Cummings Research Park, weekends are precious. Spending them on a ladder with a garden trowel isn't anyone's idea of a good time. That's where we come in.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts (a common shortcut that causes clogs downstream).</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that many homeowners miss when attempting DIY cleaning — debris backs up in the downspout, water can't exit, and the gutter overflows even though it looks clean from above.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system: hangers, seams, slope, and the fascia boards behind. We'll flag loose hangers, developing leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage before they become expensive problems. When we're done, we clean up all debris from your landscaping — your property will look better than when we arrived.</p>
{% endset %}

